@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `hxpB`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 100% of them, at 0.08 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The fork and variable columns run from 1 to 79.** Column 7, `thrS`, is a fork column carried by 88%, with a second family at 27% {S2.c7}. A branch of 31 families runs through columns 4 to 34, a parallel path carried in 11 to 12% {S2.b4}. Columns 11 to 13, `pheM` to `pheT`, are [[phenylalanine trna ligase]] {S2.c12, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 100% against 94%, and hesitates less there, 0.08 against 0.28 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 7, `thrS`, is a fork column, at 1.19 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends at column 79, `ydhL`**, a fork column carried by 72%, with `ydhF` at 46% and `sodC` at 23% {S2.c79, E}. The model names 64 to 99.6% of the fork and variable columns, fewest at column 7 {S2}.

@whole **Across the window it names 94% of genes**, 0.28 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.74 against 0.18 bits, and names fewer genes, 61% against 97% {C}.

